call_details.response:
The opponent (“x”) has no immediate winning move, but they already own two stacked pieces in column 2 and could create a strong vertical/diagonal attack if we let them add another disk there.  
By dropping an “o” in column 2 we

• land on row 3 (the only open slot in that column), immediately breaking their vertical stack;  
• create a diagonal of three of our own disks (row 5 col 4, row 4 col 3, row 3 col 2) that is only one piece away from victory;  
• occupy a valuable central column, improving our future horizontal and diagonal prospects;  
• leave the board without any reply that gives “x” an instant win on their following turn.

No other legal move simultaneously blocks the opponent’s best build-up and gives us such a strong offensive opportunity.  
Therefore the optimal play is to put our disk in column 2.

Final Answer: 2

